NAME
    id - print this session's user identity

SYNOPSIS
    id

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the calling task's user and group id as "uid=N gid=M". Numeric only
    - there is no /etc/passwd yet, so names are not resolved (that arrives with
    the login/users step).

    Identity is carried by the kernel per task and inherited across spawn, so
    running id after su reports the new user - the proof that a command runs as
    whoever started it:

        # id
        uid=0 gid=0
        # su 1000:1000
        $ id
        uid=1000 gid=1000

    A pipeline stage like any other: `id | grep uid` works.

SEE ALSO
    su, sh
